# Managed by Ansible (roles/hardening). AIDE exclusions for lamware.
#
# Only DATA and STORAGE that churn by design: container image storage, sample and
# analysis data, databases, and caches. Code, configuration and every venv stay
# monitored. Measured 2026-10-25: these paths were ~760k of the 1.07M differences
# between the April baseline and October, which made the nightly report unreadable.
#
# Container images: rebuilt hermetically from hash-locked inputs on deploy (ADR-023).
!/home/pipeline/\.local/share/containers
!/var/lib/containers
# Sample and analysis data (malware artefacts, reports, the eval corpus).
!/opt/CAPEv2/storage
!/opt/pipeline/reports
!/opt/pipeline/eval-corpus
!/opt/pipeline/harvest
!/dev/shm
# Databases.
!/var/lib/postgresql
!/data/db
# Caches and fetched build inputs (each input is hash-checked where it is used).
!/home/cape/\.cache
!/home/cape/\.npm
!/var/lib/lamware-fetch
# lamware-aide's own reports: tonight's file would be tomorrow's "added" entry.
!/var/lib/lamware-aide/reports
# Runtime and temporary state. Measured 2026-10-25 in a check 7 minutes after a
# rebaseline: these were the differences left that no deploy or package made.
!/run/user
!/run/systemd/journal/streams
!/run/lamware-aide\.lock$
!/tmp/user
!/home/[^/]+/\.ansible/tmp
!/root/\.ansible/tmp
!/var/lib/nginx/(body|proxy|fastcgi|uwsgi|scgi)
!/var/spool/lamware-notify
!/var/lib/aide/aide\.db\.(new|prev)$
# Generated every hour by root's suricata-update cron from the downloaded feeds.
# Its configuration (/etc/suricata/*.yaml, *.conf) stays monitored.
!/etc/suricata/rules
!/var/lib/suricata/update/cache
# Rewritten by the network monitor on every pass, so AIDE cannot tell an edit
# from the monitor's own write; the monitor's code and configuration stay monitored.
!/opt/network-monitor/(baseline|status)\.json$
# Detonation traffic logs and reports (inetsim): analysis data, like CAPE storage.
!/var/log/inetsim
# security-test's output and nuclei's cache. merge-check runs security-test after
# the deploy's rebaseline, so without these every PR is the next night's alert.
!/opt/security-test/results
!/root/\.cache/nuclei
!/root/\.config/nuclei/\.templates-config\.json$
# Daily housekeeping, measured in the 2026-10-26 00:00 check: apt-show-versions'
# package cache and systemd's persistent-timer stamp files (mtime only).
!/var/cache/apt-show-versions
!/var/lib/systemd/timers/stamp-
# State that scheduled jobs rewrite, enumerated from the host's timers and cron
# jobs (2026-11-04) and confirmed in the nightly checks of 10-27 to 11-04:
# apt-daily / unattended-upgrades (package lists, the package cache and its
# downloads, run stamps, PackageKit, update-notifier, the software catalog),
# fwupd-refresh (firmware metadata and its motd line), certbot's work state,
# and man-db's cache. Packages themselves stay monitored where they install
# (/usr, /etc, /boot), and an install rebaselines through the apt hook.
!/var/lib/apt/lists
!/var/cache/apt
!/var/lib/apt/periodic
!/var/lib/PackageKit
!/var/lib/update-notifier
!/var/cache/swcatalog
!/var/lib/swcatalog
!/var/cache/fwupd
!/var/lib/fwupd/metadata
!/run/motd\.d
!/var/lib/letsencrypt
!/var/cache/man
